  "texts": [
    "Most people should have their teeth professionally cleaned every six months.",
    "A professional cleaning removes plaque and hardened tartar that brushing and flossing leave behind.",
    "People with gum disease often need cleanings every three to four months.",
    "Smokers and people with diabetes have a higher risk of gum problems, so they may need cleanings more often.",
    "Most dental insurance plans cover two cleanings per year.",
    "At BrightPath Dental we use an air-polishing system that lifts stains without scraping.",
    "Our South Austin hygienists book fifty-minute appointments so nobody is rushed.",
    "In our 2025 patient survey, 68 percent of patients on a four-month schedule reported less bleeding when flossing.",
    "We send a text reminder three weeks before you are due, with a link to pick your own time.",
    "Dentists generally recommend a professional teeth cleaning every six months.",
    "Cleanings remove plaque and tartar that regular brushing and flossing cannot reach.",
    "If you have gum disease, your dentist may recommend a cleaning every three or four months.",
    "A routine cleaning usually takes 30 to 60 minutes.",
    "Dental X-rays are usually taken once a year during a cleaning visit.",
    "A fluoride treatment is often applied at the end of the cleaning.",
    "Our downtown office offers evening appointments on Tuesdays and Thursdays for people who work near the Capitol.",
    "The usual advice is to get your teeth professionally cleaned every six months.",
    "Professional cleanings get rid of the plaque and tartar your toothbrush leaves behind.",
    "Those with gum disease may need to come in every three to four months.",
    "Babies should have a first dental visit by the time they turn one.",
    "The appointment often ends with a fluoride treatment.",
    "Some researchers argue that low-risk adults could safely stretch the interval to once a year.",
    "Most patients should schedule a professional dental cleaning every six months.",
    "Patients with periodontal disease usually need cleanings every three to four months.",
    "Dental insurance typically pays for two cleanings a year.",
    "A child should see the dentist for the first time by age one.",
    "X-rays are typically taken once a year as part of a cleaning visit.",
    "A standard cleaning appointment lasts between 30 and 60 minutes.",
    "Lakeside Smiles opens at seven on weekdays so you can come in before work.",
    "Most people need a professional cleaning about every six months.",
    "A cleaning removes the plaque and tartar that daily brushing and flossing leave behind.",
    "Children should visit a dentist by age one.",
    "Expect dental X-rays roughly once a year during one of your cleanings.",
    "A routine cleaning takes about 30 to 60 minutes.",
    "Community water fluoridation has reduced tooth decay nationwide since the 1940s.",
    "For most adults, a professional cleaning twice a year is the standard recommendation.",
    "During a cleaning, the hygienist removes tartar and plaque that brushing at home misses.",
    "Smokers and people with diabetes have a higher risk of gum problems and may need more frequent cleanings.",
    "Children should have their first dental visit by their first birthday.",
    "Most offices take X-rays about once a year at a cleaning appointment.",
    "Many hygienists finish the cleaning with a fluoride treatment.",
    "Electric toothbrushes with pressure sensors can help people who brush too hard."
